      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 35: 🟡 The comment says callbacks must not call back into the same instance, but the implementation uses std::recursive_mutex, which allows same-thread reentry while a libyrs transaction is being committed. That can start nested transactions from observers and risk libyrs state corruption/abort. Prefer a non-recursive mutex plus invoking copied callbacks after the transaction/lock, or add an explicit reentrancy guard that rejects mutation from callbacks.",
